# Python bytecode (test fixtures import the shared spectral_terrain module)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Model run outputs. Any run whose config sets output.directory writes results/<run>/ beside the
# config; tests/config_schema makes them routinely because it runs the REFERENCE config.yaml unmodified
# (which is the point of that arm -- validating the config as shipped).
#
# SCOPED ON PURPOSE, not a blanket `results/`. benchmark/adaptive_dt/results/ holds TRACKED csv
# summaries (adapt_bench_spinup.csv, adapt_bench_transient.csv -- the record of those benchmarks) and
# has no local ignore rule, so a bare `results/`, which matches at any depth, would silently stop new
# benchmark data there from ever being committed. Verified with git check-ignore both ways.
# (benchmark/esquibel/results/scaling/ is separately ignored by its own pre-existing .gitignore; that
# is the repo's existing choice there, not this rule's doing.)
/results/
tests/*/results/
